ongoing and widespread flooding in  eastern australia where people have lost  lives and livelihoods to the rising  water  human-caused climate change is  increasing the risk of this kind of  event  now a dire warning from the un's  intergovernmental panel on climate  change that over 3 billion people nearly  half the planet's population are living  in harm's way because of global warming  i've seen many scientific reports in my  time but nothing like this  today's ipcc report is an atlas of human  suffering  and the damning indictment of failed  climate leadership  with fact upon fact this report reveals  how people on the planet are getting  clobbered by climate change  as wildfires burn in argentina the un  predicts unavoidable and irreversible  impacts on humans animals and the  ecosystems they rely on  even if temperature rises are limited to  a best case scenario  and as recent flooding in the west  midlands shows this is not a problem  limited to far away places  the hard bit is working out how to adapt  to the changes that are already here and  the ones that are predicted to come in  this country for example that might mean  better land management it might mean  more flood defenses or even moving some  communities away from the water  altogether  whatever the solution it's going to be  expensive and the longer we wait the  more expensive it's going to get  still the report warns as climate change  drives food and water scarcity and even  conflict  some people and places are already being  pushed beyond their ability to adapt no  matter what is spent in the future  i think it's an incredibly uh stark  warning it's a grim warning and  you know i would argue this is another  code red for humanity and what this  report says to us is that the impact on  lives and livelihoods and nature are far  worse than were originally anticipated  and not only that but those who are  affected the most disproportionately are  those who are most uh vulnerable  those vulnerable communities need more  help and quickly from rich nations  everywhere at the same time as global  efforts to reduce carbon emissions are  also stepped up  a huge challenge that the world we are  told must rise to  hannah thomas peter sky news
 

